    {
      "title": "Hangul Alphabet",
      "explanation": "Korean uses Hangul (한글), a phonetic alphabet created in 1443. It has 14 consonants and 10 vowels, combined into syllable blocks. It is considered one of the most scientific writing systems.",
      "examples": ["ㅏ (a), ㅣ (i), ㅗ (o), ㅜ (u)", "가 (ga) = g + a", "한 (han) = h + a + n"]
